WEBVTT

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.733
<i>What's this feeling I have,</i>
<i>as if I'm looking forward to...</i>

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:25.939
<i>... somebody firing off his</i>
<i>missiles and ending everything?</i>

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:31.378
<i>Is it a bad thing, or is this normal?</i>

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:37.884
<i>I can't figure it out on my</i>
<i>own, so somebody tell me!</i>

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:43.490
<i>And that person I love has once again...</i>

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>... gone far away without anybody noticing.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:56.103
<i>Where have my dreams gone since then?</i>

00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:01.775
<i>I could swear that they</i>
<i>were right here long ago.</i>

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:07.814
<i>We had a love that set our hearts on fire.</i>

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:20.784
<i>Let's take back that feeling we had back then!</i>

00:01:39.212 --> 00:01:41.373
Everything's come together.

00:01:42.949 --> 00:01:43.717
Mr. Tsuchida!

00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:45.318
Well done, well done!

00:01:45.318 --> 00:01:47.387
But your stance still needs work!

00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:51.391
Hold the sacred staff lightly,
swinging it as if you're sliding.

00:01:51.391 --> 00:01:52.826
Mr. Tsuchida!

00:01:52.826 --> 00:01:54.623
Are you all right?

00:01:56.329 --> 00:01:58.932
You shouldn't overdo it.

00:01:58.932 --> 00:02:01.201
Okay, hold it right there!

00:02:01.201 --> 00:02:02.803
Peace!

00:02:02.803 --> 00:02:04.371
That was mean!

00:02:04.371 --> 00:02:06.873
What're you doing, Sakuya?

00:02:06.873 --> 00:02:10.577
I have a camera. What do you think I'm doing?

00:02:10.577 --> 00:02:15.115
I just thought I'd take
pictures of our summer together.

00:02:15.115 --> 00:02:17.350
To remember my summer with you.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.085
Sakuya...

00:02:19.085 --> 00:02:23.623
I'm gonna take pictures
until you're done practicing.

00:02:23.623 --> 00:02:26.217
Please, go right ahead.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:46.304
I really don't understand
what that girl's doing...

00:02:56.089 --> 00:02:59.025
What?

00:02:59.025 --> 00:03:02.095
Wh-What was that you said just now, Sasami?

00:03:02.095 --> 00:03:06.589
I said, my friend Yugi disappeared
all of a sudden yesterday!

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.875
Did she say "Yugi"?

00:03:22.048 --> 00:03:25.418
What's wrong, Ayeka?

00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:29.256
The evil one who attacked the Masaki
Shrine recently was also named Yugi.

00:03:29.256 --> 00:03:32.359
Huh? No way! It's just some coincidence!

00:03:32.359 --> 00:03:36.396
Sasami, let's find out for sure
whether or not it's a coincidence.

00:03:36.396 --> 00:03:38.489
Wait here a moment!

00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:41.902
She was something like this...

00:03:41.902 --> 00:03:45.238
Her eyes are kinda like this, right, Ryo-Ohki?

00:03:45.238 --> 00:03:49.242
Sasami! Is this the "Yugi" girl you met?

00:03:49.242 --> 00:03:53.144
No, that's not her! My Yugi looks like this!

00:03:54.748 --> 00:03:57.551
This is getting us nowhere...

00:03:57.551 --> 00:03:59.178
I know what to do!

00:04:00.887 --> 00:04:02.989
So, what do you want?

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:06.893
Washu, please show
Sasami those visuals of Yugi.

00:04:06.893 --> 00:04:09.191
Those? Sure.

00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:17.826
Look! This is the Yugi that
attacked the Masaki Shrine!

00:04:25.412 --> 00:04:27.447
Sasami...

00:04:27.447 --> 00:04:29.015
Sasami?

00:04:29.015 --> 00:04:30.483
- Yugi?
- Sasami... Sasami...

00:04:30.483 --> 00:04:33.646
- It... It has to be some kind of mistake!
- Sasami... Sasami...

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:44.960
That'll do it.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:50.170
Come on, try to be a little more relaxed.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.105
The way you're moving is a little unnatural.

00:04:52.105 --> 00:04:55.275
But when you say that,
I think about it even more...

00:04:55.275 --> 00:05:00.413
All right. Stay with me until
I can get a good shot, instead.

00:05:00.413 --> 00:05:02.616
Uh... Sure.

00:05:02.616 --> 00:05:05.819
That's a nice camera. Is it your dad's?

00:05:05.819 --> 00:05:07.787
No, it's mine.

00:05:07.787 --> 00:05:12.425
Really? Your family
must be pretty rich, Sakuya.

00:05:12.425 --> 00:05:14.394
Huh? Why's that?

00:05:14.394 --> 00:05:17.931
I mean, that's a really
high-quality camera, right?

00:05:17.931 --> 00:05:20.266
Really?

00:05:20.266 --> 00:05:24.738
Speaking of which, what is
it that your parents do, again?

00:05:24.738 --> 00:05:26.239
My parents?

00:05:26.239 --> 00:05:29.609
Yeah. I've never heard you talk about them.

00:05:29.609 --> 00:05:34.080
Oh, I get it! You want to
meet my parents, Tenchi!

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.052
N-No... Th-That's not how I meant it.

00:05:39.052 --> 00:05:44.124
Forget about that. Let's go take
some pictures at the park this time!

00:05:44.124 --> 00:05:47.116
Huh? Hey, Sakuya!

00:05:56.403 --> 00:06:00.271
Um... What is all this, Sister?

00:06:02.108 --> 00:06:05.111
<i>3,500 years ago, Yugi...</i>

00:06:05.111 --> 00:06:08.948
...brought Jurai to the brink of destruction!

00:06:08.948 --> 00:06:12.752
And she is also the evil one
who attacked the Masaki Shrine!

00:06:12.752 --> 00:06:15.822
And to think that she also
had you in her clutches, Sasami!

00:06:15.822 --> 00:06:20.627
No! I can't believe that Yugi
would do something like that!

00:06:20.627 --> 00:06:24.364
She can't be the Yugi that I know!

00:06:24.364 --> 00:06:27.734
No, Sasami! You're being deceived!

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:29.167
She can't be...

00:06:36.376 --> 00:06:37.866
Ryo-Ohki!

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.185
Ryo-Ohki!

00:06:45.185 --> 00:06:47.921
My traps are foolproof.

00:06:47.921 --> 00:06:50.323
Sister, you don't have to go this far!

00:06:50.323 --> 00:06:54.527
Sasami! Right now in the Masaki house,
Lord Tenchi and Mihoshi and Kiyone...

00:06:54.527 --> 00:06:58.131
...and Ryoko, but who
cares about her, are all gone!

00:06:58.131 --> 00:07:00.900
I am the only one who can protect the house!

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.402
That's right.

00:07:02.402 --> 00:07:05.530
And we'll do what little we can to help!

00:07:06.372 --> 00:07:08.441
All right, we can't leave it at this.

00:07:08.441 --> 00:07:12.172
We're going to build traps
to protect the house itself!

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.683
Oh, dear!

00:07:16.683 --> 00:07:18.518
It can't be her, right, Ryo-Ohki?

00:07:18.518 --> 00:07:21.954
Yugi wouldn't do anything bad like that, right?

00:07:23.857 --> 00:07:26.726
A little more to the right, Tenchi!

00:07:26.726 --> 00:07:28.628
Uh... Whose right?

00:07:28.628 --> 00:07:31.164
The hand you hold your chopsticks in.

00:07:31.164 --> 00:07:32.332
Yeah, right there!

00:07:32.332 --> 00:07:34.834
Ready? Here goes!

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:38.071
I'm sorry! I blinked!

00:07:38.071 --> 00:07:41.474
I'll take another one, then.

00:07:41.474 --> 00:07:43.109
Do you want me to take one of you this time?

00:07:43.109 --> 00:07:47.046
No, that's okay. I wanna
take one with the two of us in it.

00:07:47.046 --> 00:07:49.071
This ain't good...

00:07:49.983 --> 00:07:50.784
Well?

00:07:50.784 --> 00:07:51.985
Still no movement.

00:07:51.985 --> 00:07:53.386
Um...

00:07:53.386 --> 00:07:55.488
I'm sorry, could you do me a favor?

00:07:55.488 --> 00:07:57.957
- S-Sure! How can we help you?
- S-Sure! How can we help you?

00:07:57.957 --> 00:08:00.755
Okay, are you ready? Here goes!

00:08:01.728 --> 00:08:03.855
Wait a second!

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:09.399
Put your arm here.

00:08:10.737 --> 00:08:12.830
Okay, say "cheese"!

00:08:14.941 --> 00:08:17.243
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

00:08:17.243 --> 00:08:18.211
Oh, damn!

00:08:18.211 --> 00:08:19.769
Come back here!

00:08:20.947 --> 00:08:25.850
Actually, Sakuya, why do you
want to take pictures all of a sudden?

00:08:27.353 --> 00:08:29.289
I wonder why?

00:08:29.289 --> 00:08:31.691
I'm not really sure why, myself.

00:08:31.691 --> 00:08:32.859
Sakuya?

00:08:32.859 --> 00:08:33.827
What?

00:08:33.827 --> 00:08:36.396
You're from Tokyo, right?

00:08:36.396 --> 00:08:38.598
Why ask that?

00:08:38.598 --> 00:08:42.435
Well, now that I think about it,
I don't know anything at all about you.

00:08:42.435 --> 00:08:45.461
Do you live with your parents?

00:08:46.339 --> 00:08:47.473
I don't know.

00:08:47.473 --> 00:08:51.744
Hey, Tenchi, let's have some ice cream!

00:08:51.744 --> 00:08:52.846
C'mon, let's go!

00:08:52.846 --> 00:08:54.837
Uh... Sure.

00:09:08.828 --> 00:09:11.661
Looks like this isn't
gonna be easy to figure out...

00:09:15.802 --> 00:09:21.172
I come home early for once, but
the house seems different, somehow...

00:09:22.108 --> 00:09:27.513
This is a warning.
No one may come any closer.

00:09:27.513 --> 00:09:30.744
Come on, now. What kind of joke is this?

00:09:32.418 --> 00:09:35.182
I did warn him...

00:09:36.389 --> 00:09:38.191
You two on a date, Miss?

00:09:38.191 --> 00:09:39.192
Yeah!

00:09:39.192 --> 00:09:41.628
No kiddin'. It's nice to be young.

00:09:41.628 --> 00:09:43.963
Did you go out on dates
when you were young, mister?

00:09:43.963 --> 00:09:47.233
No, when I was young,
even if you liked a girl,

00:09:47.233 --> 00:09:49.502
you couldn't hang out with her.

00:09:49.502 --> 00:09:50.603
Really?

00:09:50.603 --> 00:09:54.140
Hey, it's on the house today. Here!

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:56.506
Thanks, mister!

00:09:59.145 --> 00:10:02.637
They'd never think that
I'd come in from the back...

00:10:04.217 --> 00:10:06.447
I've spotted an intruder!

00:10:09.856 --> 00:10:11.721
And that's that.

00:10:14.661 --> 00:10:18.097
If you eat it this way, the cold feels great!

00:10:18.097 --> 00:10:20.190
I guess I'll give it a try.

00:10:22.435 --> 00:10:24.804
That's cold!

00:10:24.804 --> 00:10:28.975
Man, my shoulders are
stiff today for some reason...

00:10:28.975 --> 00:10:31.711
I'm sorry. I've been making
you do all this weird stuff.

00:10:31.711 --> 00:10:35.248
That's okay. Souvenir
pictures are always like that.

00:10:35.248 --> 00:10:36.683
Souvenir pictures?

00:10:36.683 --> 00:10:39.886
Yeah, it's always like that when you
take pictures with a bunch of people.

00:10:39.886 --> 00:10:43.489
You blink, or when you worry
about making a strange face,

00:10:43.489 --> 00:10:46.025
you make an even stranger one.

00:10:46.025 --> 00:10:49.595
Sakuya... You've never had a
souvenir picture taken before?

00:10:49.595 --> 00:10:52.665
Huh? Uh, I don't know...

00:10:52.665 --> 00:10:54.033
You don't know?

00:10:54.033 --> 00:10:58.137
But whenever you go on a trip with
your family or out on a school picnic,

00:10:58.137 --> 00:11:00.640
you take a group picture, right?

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:01.674
I don't know.

00:11:01.674 --> 00:11:03.676
You don't know, Sakuya?

00:11:03.676 --> 00:11:06.279
Don't you have a scrapbook
or something at home?

00:11:06.279 --> 00:11:09.482
You know, pictures of
your family or something?

00:11:09.482 --> 00:11:11.517
I don't know...

00:11:11.517 --> 00:11:16.155
My house... My family... My memories...

00:11:16.155 --> 00:11:20.326
I don't know. I... I don't know.

00:11:20.326 --> 00:11:22.317
Sakuya...

00:11:51.424 --> 00:11:53.016
Catch!

00:11:55.294 --> 00:11:57.592
Th-That's the village treasure!

00:12:02.869 --> 00:12:09.142
Don't worry. I'll put
your treasure to good use.

00:12:09.142 --> 00:12:10.209
What will you do with it?

00:12:10.209 --> 00:12:13.880
I'm not sure. Sell it for a fortune
on the black market, maybe?

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:14.847
What?!

00:12:14.847 --> 00:12:18.551
Or maybe use it as a target in the
Galactic Sharpshooting Competition!

00:12:18.551 --> 00:12:22.180
Hey, I know! I'll use it as a
weight stone for when I make pickles!

00:12:23.322 --> 00:12:25.347
Stop it!

00:12:26.893 --> 00:12:29.028
You damn pirate! Drop dead!

00:12:29.028 --> 00:12:31.564
We'll never hand over the village treasure!

00:12:31.564 --> 00:12:34.158
Put down the treasure and get out of here!

00:12:36.302 --> 00:12:39.032
You talk big, boy.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:45.411
Relax, I don't hurt kids.

00:12:45.411 --> 00:12:47.345
I ain't a kid!

00:12:49.515 --> 00:12:52.618
You little bastard! I went easy
on you because you're a kid,

00:12:52.618 --> 00:12:55.610
but you just asked for it!

00:13:01.627 --> 00:13:03.356
What's wrong, Ryoko?

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.658
Ryoko!

00:13:16.242 --> 00:13:18.403
Tenchi...

00:13:29.222 --> 00:13:31.690
So once again, Ryoko's already left, huh?

00:13:32.959 --> 00:13:35.628
She's running rings around us...

00:13:35.628 --> 00:13:38.364
Look out! Enemy attack from the rear!

00:13:38.364 --> 00:13:40.992
All cannons, emergency deploy to aft!

00:13:48.975 --> 00:13:52.011
Look out! He's gonna pin
your arms behind your back!

00:13:52.011 --> 00:13:54.981
That's sneaky, Drillworm Bazooka Man!

00:13:54.981 --> 00:13:59.619
Well, Policeman, the
entire universe is now ours!

00:13:59.619 --> 00:14:03.456
What're you saying? I, Policeman,
will protect peace in the universe!

00:14:03.456 --> 00:14:06.687
Feel the Frantic Togetherness Kick!

00:14:07.393 --> 00:14:10.829
Long live Leader Wargon!

00:14:12.165 --> 00:14:15.293
I'll remember this!

00:14:15.368 --> 00:14:17.870
Did you protect peace in the universe?

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.240
It'd be nice if you could do something
about peace in this universe, too.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:22.975
Don't be mad, Kiyone!

00:14:22.975 --> 00:14:26.946
I was bored because
I can't watch "Policeman"!

00:14:26.946 --> 00:14:29.048
You looked like you
were having plenty of fun...

00:14:29.048 --> 00:14:31.584
Anyway, when did you buy all this stuff?

00:14:31.584 --> 00:14:35.288
What're you trying to do,
fill up the cockpit with dolls?

00:14:35.288 --> 00:14:37.779
I'm gonna throw 'em all into space.

00:14:42.061 --> 00:14:44.964
Please, Mihoshi! Don't
throw away my Policemen!

00:14:44.964 --> 00:14:48.701
I'll only play with my Policeman
dolls three times a day, okay?

00:14:48.701 --> 00:14:51.637
Twice a day! No, once, so please!

00:14:51.637 --> 00:14:54.128
Please, Kiyone...

00:14:55.174 --> 00:14:58.744
The next time we're off-duty,
what say we go to Earth?

00:14:58.744 --> 00:14:59.946
Sure!

00:14:59.946 --> 00:15:02.615
Great! I can watch "Policeman"!

00:15:02.615 --> 00:15:07.553
And I can pick up the "Policeman"
shows that Sasami's been taping for me!

00:15:07.553 --> 00:15:10.923
But only after we get
permission from the Chief.

00:15:10.923 --> 00:15:14.493
Let's go ask! Let's go ask right away!

00:15:14.493 --> 00:15:16.629
Maybe I'll watch "Policeman," too.

00:15:16.629 --> 00:15:20.793
Let's watch it! Let's watch it! It's so great!

00:15:26.706 --> 00:15:30.243
Look, look! This face you're
making is so weird, Tenchi!

00:15:30.243 --> 00:15:32.912
Look who's talking, Sakuya.

00:15:32.912 --> 00:15:35.281
Hey! T-Time out!

00:15:35.281 --> 00:15:38.876
N-Not this one! Forget about this one!

00:15:45.224 --> 00:15:47.360
Sakuya, is orange juice okay?

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.225
Sure.

00:15:53.299 --> 00:15:54.867
Tenchi...

00:15:54.867 --> 00:15:57.028
Keep this one on your desk, okay?

00:15:58.371 --> 00:16:00.396
Thanks.

00:16:03.909 --> 00:16:05.478
What's wrong?

00:16:05.478 --> 00:16:08.614
Oh, it's nothing.

00:16:08.614 --> 00:16:12.018
You're thinking about that lady
from Okayama who came yesterday?

00:16:12.018 --> 00:16:14.086
No, that's not it.

00:16:14.086 --> 00:16:15.688
Liar.

00:16:15.688 --> 00:16:19.225
It's written all over your face. You
want to go back to Okayama right away.

00:16:19.225 --> 00:16:23.896
Remember, you promised
to spend the summer with me.

00:16:23.896 --> 00:16:29.201
Anyway, I don't think going back
to Okayama would do any good.

00:16:29.201 --> 00:16:30.303
Sakuya?

00:16:30.303 --> 00:16:33.205
Everybody has their own life to lead.

00:16:33.205 --> 00:16:38.210
I mean, nobody else can live
Ryoko's and Ayeka's lives for them.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:39.478
Right?

00:16:39.478 --> 00:16:41.847
Well, that may be true,

00:16:41.847 --> 00:16:44.684
but Okayama's my hometown.

00:16:44.684 --> 00:16:49.822
I mean, you sometimes want to go back
to your hometown, too, right, Sakuya?

00:16:49.822 --> 00:16:51.691
My... hometown?

00:16:51.691 --> 00:16:54.216
My... home?

00:16:55.561 --> 00:16:58.431
Sakuya, what do your parents do, again?

00:16:58.431 --> 00:17:01.334
Do you live with your parents, Sakuya?

00:17:01.334 --> 00:17:04.737
Sakuya, don't you have a
scrapbook or something at home?

00:17:04.737 --> 00:17:07.069
You know, pictures of your family or whatever?

00:17:10.042 --> 00:17:13.779
My house... My family...

00:17:13.779 --> 00:17:16.270
My memories...

00:17:27.626 --> 00:17:29.150
Sakuya?

00:17:30.229 --> 00:17:32.857
Sakuya? Sakuya, snap out of it!

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.268
Tenchi...

00:17:36.268 --> 00:17:40.072
Thank goodness... What the heck happened?

00:17:40.072 --> 00:17:42.408
Tenchi, please...

00:17:42.408 --> 00:17:46.545
Just... Just look at me!
Don't look at anyone else!

00:17:46.545 --> 00:17:48.514
Don't go anywhere!

00:17:48.514 --> 00:17:50.883
What's wrong, Sakuya?

00:17:50.883 --> 00:17:55.911
I... I mean, I...

00:18:00.559 --> 00:18:02.424
Sakuya!

00:18:10.836 --> 00:18:14.397
They'd never think that
I'd come home over the lake!

00:18:15.708 --> 00:18:17.476
What the heck's this?

00:18:17.476 --> 00:18:20.274
- Oh, my! A villain!
- A villain!

00:18:28.621 --> 00:18:32.057
It sounds like the evil
one fell into one of my traps.

00:18:37.229 --> 00:18:42.134
Yugi... Was it really you who
attacked the Masaki Shrine?

00:18:42.134 --> 00:18:46.539
No, it couldn't be... You and I are friends!

00:18:46.539 --> 00:18:49.906
Sasami, I thought we were friends...

00:18:52.011 --> 00:18:56.015
Come to my place!
We can live there together!

00:18:56.015 --> 00:18:59.118
You're my friend, aren't you, Sasami?

00:18:59.118 --> 00:19:03.155
What're you saying, Yugi? We're still kids.

00:19:03.155 --> 00:19:05.791
We can't live by ourselves.

00:19:05.791 --> 00:19:07.725
Fine! See if I care!

00:19:08.461 --> 00:19:12.231
Come to me, Sasami. I'll be waiting.

00:19:12.231 --> 00:19:15.200
It's lonely, being by myself.

00:19:15.768 --> 00:19:20.039
It's almost time for my land to come
out into the open, Matori! Tsugaru!

00:19:20.039 --> 00:19:22.441
- Yes, Ma'am!
- Yes, Ma'am!

00:19:22.441 --> 00:19:25.308
I'll begin preparations for our departure.

00:19:43.796 --> 00:19:45.195
What the...?

00:20:20.332 --> 00:20:22.134
My house?

00:20:22.134 --> 00:20:24.136
My family?

00:20:24.136 --> 00:20:26.305
My memories?

00:20:26.305 --> 00:20:28.674
I don't have any of those.

00:20:28.674 --> 00:20:33.012
Just like Tenchi has a house,
a family, and memories,

00:20:33.012 --> 00:20:38.143
I ought to have a house,
a family, and memories, too...

00:20:38.851 --> 00:20:43.622
But I... I don't have anything...

00:20:43.622 --> 00:20:49.862
I don't remember anything
before I met Tenchi... Why?

00:20:49.862 --> 00:20:51.989
Why can't I remember?

00:20:59.438 --> 00:21:02.708
Tenchi...

00:21:02.708 --> 00:21:07.379
Help me, Tenchi...

00:21:07.379 --> 00:21:09.404
Help me...

00:21:36.041 --> 00:21:39.645
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:39.645 --> 00:21:43.549
<i>Sleeping late, staying up late,</i>
<i>and napping all the time!</i>

00:21:43.549 --> 00:21:47.152
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:47.152 --> 00:21:51.090
<i>Sneaking bites to eat, midnight</i>
<i>snacks, and pouring tea on my rice!</i>

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:54.593
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:54.593 --> 00:21:58.564
<i>Playing video games and singing karaoke!</i>

00:21:58.564 --> 00:22:01.900
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:05.904
<i>Lying in the sun and taking baths outside!</i>

00:22:05.904 --> 00:22:08.040
<i>- Taking side trips!</i>
<i>- Gossiping!</i>

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:09.975
<i>- Taking long baths</i>
<i>- Wasting my money!</i>

00:22:09.975 --> 00:22:11.477
<i>- Being a busybody!</i>
<i>- Talking forever on the phone!</i>

00:22:11.477 --> 00:22:17.316
<i>- Unrequited love!</i>
<i>- Stealing other people's men!</i>

00:22:17.316 --> 00:22:21.420
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:24.690
<i>no matter how old I get!</i>

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:28.227
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it,</i>

00:22:28.227 --> 00:22:32.926
<i>even if I die, change shape, or get reborn!</i>

00:22:45.044 --> 00:22:46.412
This is Ayeka.

00:22:46.412 --> 00:22:49.081
Ryoko hasn't been back
since she went into space.

00:22:49.081 --> 00:22:53.085
Mihoshi and Kiyone haven't
been back since they left for Pluto.

00:22:53.085 --> 00:22:56.955
And Lord Tenchi hasn't been
back since he left for Tokyo.

00:22:56.955 --> 00:22:59.692
As the only one left, all I can do is...

00:22:59.692 --> 00:23:03.462
Yes! With Lord Tenchi gone,
I'll protect the Masaki residence!

00:23:03.462 --> 00:23:05.597
I'll get right down to business!

00:23:05.597 --> 00:23:10.864
Next time on <i>Tenchi in Tokyo:</i>
"Here, There, and Everywhere."
